not concerned with them. But recently, I felt like my anxiety has developed into a new level. I got so damn anxious for every day stuff."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_921c66a469a2d000", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_403aa7e3cbe150d2", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "  **TL;DR's** 1st: Why would parents be like this to their kids? Thinking they need to be treated like a king, or willing to say they wish their kids would just vanish isn't normal parenting, right? Or am I just insane? I know I'd never do that.", "candidate_role": "counterevidence", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as a boundary case or counterexample.", "display_order": 3, "excerpt_id": "EXC_921c66a469a2d000", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_403aa7e3cbe150d2", "speaker_id": null, "text": "  **TL;DR's** 1st: Why would parents be like this to their kids? Thinking they need to be treated like a king, or willing to say they wish their kids would just vanish isn't normal parenting, right? Or am I just insane? I know I'd never do that."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 4, "excerpt_id": "EXC_791472689efe2ec1", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_414031feb440366e", "speaker_id": null, "text": "&#x200B; **Heyyyyyy. ** So Just wanted to introduce myself. I'm a young lady who suffers from Complex PTSD and just want to reach out to be part of a community to get some help while also helping others. Supporting other PTSD victims is something that has helped me heal."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_ce0cd8dc1c9ef5cb", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_979ad0e8ca295fb8", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "My daughter's father I was with for 5 years on and off. He was not abusive the first year, however when he became so I left and found out two weeks later I was pregnant. Of course he begged and pleaded for a second chance, and I believed that my daughter deserved me to at least give it a shot. I came back and surprise surprise it was worse than it ever was. I stuck it out until he disappeared for the eleventeenth time on a drunken bender, I checked my Facebook to find some scumbag girl who was dating one of his best friends was posting horrific, nasty, way out shit about me.", "candidate_role": "support", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as direct support for the interpretation.", "display_order": 5, "excerpt_id": "EXC_ce0cd8dc1c9ef5cb", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_979ad0e8ca295fb8", "speaker_id": null, "text": "My daughter's father I was with for 5 years on and off. He was not abusive the first year, however when he became so I left and found out two weeks later I was pregnant. Of course he begged and pleaded for a second chance, and I believed that my daughter deserved me to at least give it a shot. I came back and surprise surprise it was worse than it ever was. I stuck it out until he disappeared for the eleventeenth time on a drunken bender, I checked my Facebook to find some scumbag girl who was dating one of his best friends was posting horrific, nasty, way out shit about me."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_4689db38872d614e", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_a0a04ebb37368892", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "It is having a major strain on our relationship as he obviously wants to be involved but essentially I am unloading all my worry onto him. I am really unsure how to move forwards from here. If I think I am being irrational and hold in my anxiety, he says I am not communicating with him about it. If I open up and tell him, I feel like I am a burden and it makes me feel guilty and pretty low that I'm feeling this way. Any advice would be appreciated!", "candidate_role": "support", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as direct support for the interpretation.", "display_order": 6, "excerpt_id": "EXC_4689db38872d614e", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_a0a04ebb37368892", "speaker_id": null, "text": "It is having a major strain on our relationship as he obviously wants to be involved but essentially I am unloading all my worry onto him. I am really unsure how to move forwards from here. If I think I am being irrational and hold in my anxiety, he says I am not communicating with him about it. If I open up and tell him, I feel like I am a burden and it makes me feel guilty and pretty low that I'm feeling this way. Any advice would be appreciated!"}], "item_id": "DJI_8f76cfc184ed3e8c", "item_schema_version": "direction-j-evaluator-item-v1", "output_id": "OUT_8f76cfc184ed3e8c", "packet_id": "PKT_7f84587791a72ece", "proposed_interpretation": {"boundary_conditions": ["The excerpts describe stress in the context of relationships (EXC_4689db38872d614e, EXC_ce0cd8dc1c9ef5cb), anxiety (EXC_755d923f078333a9), and trauma (EXC_791472689efe2ec1)", "The excerpts suggest that stress can be caused by external factors such as abusive relationships (EXC_ce0cd8dc1c9ef5cb) or internal factors such as anxiety (EXC_755d923f078333a9)"], "claim": "Stress is described in the context of relationships, anxiety, and trauma.", "explanation": "The excerpts suggest that stress can be caused by both external factors such as abusive relationships and internal factors such as anxiety. However, there is also a counterexample in EXC_921c66a469a2d000 where the speaker questions their own sanity.", "theme_id": "THM_8f76cfc184ed3e8c", "theme_name": "Stress in context"}, "research_question": "How do people describe and contextualize experiences of stress?", "source_coverage": {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 3, "candidate_cited_source_count": 3, "coverage_note": "Counts describe only this restricted private packet.", "presented_excerpt_count": 6, "presented_source_count": 6, "sampling_frame_excerpt_count": 6, "sampling_frame_so